Linux v6.12, drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/
Sources: https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/+/v6.12/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/
Filename underscores replace source path slashes. Original licenses preserved.
ramht: fixed display hash and parent-relative binding.
usergf119: six-word VRAM DMA object.
gp102, ramgp102: physical capacity and reserved ranges.
HOST push encoding: upstream/display/nvkm_engine_disp_nv50.c nv50_disp_dmac_push.
instmem nv50: slow PRAMIN read window transport, adapted with bounds and restore.
bar gf100/gm107: PCI index 3 is NVKM BAR2; VM context and busy registers.
mmu vmmgf100/vmmgp100: instance +200 PDB descriptor and +208 VA limit; VER2/page flags.
